2. TIMING AND DIRECTION CHANGES
All clips loop over 40 ticks at 60 Hz (2/3 second). Eight-cel clips hold [5,5,5,5,5,5,5,5] ticks. Original DL7 keeps holds [5,7,8,5,5,5,5], starts [0,5,12,20,25,30,35], and source samples [0,5,15,20,25,30,35]. Do not invent an eighth DL drawing.
D uses the drawing count, start ticks and holds listed above; any reduced-cel retiming is not exact source-phase alignment. Do not synthesize removed drawings. D has reduced right-leg articulation; spot-check its loop and turns in gameplay before adopting it.
Preserve normalized cycle time on heading changes. Compute q=(elapsed_seconds*60)%40 and select the destination clip frame whose start_tick <= q < start_tick+hold. Never copy the old drawing index and never reset the clock when turning. Keep a fractional accumulator rather than relying on engine frame rate.
New source-guide samples were checked at ticks 0,5,10,15,20,25,30,35, with tick40 excluded as the duplicate loop endpoint. Proxy source events: right release6, left contact14, left release25, right contact33. These are joint-guide proxies, NOT verified painted sole contacts or permission to foot-lock sprites.

3. REVIEW MEDIA AND LIMITS
Run_Eightway_Compass.png: all eight headings at cycle tick0. Run_Eightway_Contact.png: eight common timeline samples per heading; DL can reuse a cel at adjacent samples.
Run_Eightway_DirectionSwitch_60Hz.mp4: 60Hz output, continuous cycle, heading switch every47ticks, clockwise then reverse. One fixed display scale derived from each clip PPU and stored pivot; no per-frame silhouette fitting. The baseline marks the stored actor root, not a universal ground-contact line. Ground-plane depth projects feet above/below this line; that alone does not prove floating.
Old DR/UL elevated lantern carry, DL arm variation, new low carry, body scale, vertical registration and drawn phase differences remain visible. The preview intentionally exposes those transitions. U has restrained upper-body motion. R includes producer-baked integer pelvis stabilization; do not apply it again. Existing diagonal assets remain byte-unchanged. L includes documented alpha-only cleanup of three external sword fragments.

